#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This lesson walks through the use of classical optimization loops to feed "
"parameters into quantum calculations."
msgstr ""
"Pelajaran ini membimbing penggunaan gelung pengoptimuman klasik untuk "
"menghantar parameter ke dalam pengiraan kuantum."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optimization loops"
msgstr "Gelung pengoptimuman"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/variational-algorithm-"
"design/optimization-loops.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""
"<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/variational-algorithm-"
"design/optimization-loops.ipynb\" />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore nabla */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore nabla */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"During this lesson, we will learn how to use an *optimizer* to iteratively "
"explore the parameterized quantum states of our ansatz:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam pelajaran ini, kita akan belajar cara menggunakan *pengoptimum* untuk "
"meneroka keadaan kuantum berparameter pada ansatz kita secara berulang:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bootstrap an optimization loop\n"
msgstr "Mulakan gelung pengoptimuman\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Understand trade-offs while using local and global optimizers\n"
msgstr ""
"Fahami pertukaran rugi-untung semasa menggunakan pengoptimum lokal dan "
"global\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Explore barren plateaus and how to avoid them\n"
msgstr "Terokai dataran tandus dan cara mengelakkannya\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At a high level, optimizers are central to exploring our search space. The "
"optimizer uses cost function evaluations to select the next set of "
"parameters in a variational loop, and repeats the process until it reaches a"
" stable state. At this stage, an optimal set of parameter values "
"$\\vec\\theta^*$ is returned.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara ringkas, pengoptimum adalah teras kepada penerokaan ruang carian "
"kita. Pengoptimum menggunakan penilaian fungsi kos untuk memilih set "
"parameter seterusnya dalam gelung variasikal, dan mengulangi proses itu "
"sehingga mencapai keadaan stabil. Pada peringkat ini, set nilai parameter "
"optimum $\\vec\\theta^*$ dikembalikan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A diagram of some important factors in optimization, including barren "
"plateaus, gradient vs gradient-free optimizers, and "
"bootstrapping.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-"
"design/optimization-loops/optimization-workflow.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Rajah beberapa faktor penting dalam pengoptimuman, termasuk dataran "
"tandus, pengoptimum berasaskan kecerunan lwn. tanpa kecerunan, dan "
"pemulaan.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-"
"design/optimization-loops/optimization-workflow.svg)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Local and Global Optimizers {#local-and-global-optimizers}"
msgstr "Pengoptimum Lokal dan Global {#local-and-global-optimizers}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll first set up our problem before exploring each optimizer class. We "
"will start with a circuit containing eight variational parameters:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan sediakan masalah kita terlebih dahulu sebelum meneroka setiap "
"kelas pengoptimum. Kita akan mulakan dengan litar yang mengandungi lapan "
"parameter variasikal:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-"
"algorithm-design/optimization-loops/extracted-"
"outputs/15cf7810-1d25-4c54-aff0-91d3a0c51cec-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output sel kod sebelumnya](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-"
"design/optimization-loops/extracted-"
"outputs/15cf7810-1d25-4c54-aff0-91d3a0c51cec-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Local Optimizers {#local-optimizers}"
msgstr "Pengoptimum Lokal {#local-optimizers}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Local optimizers search for a point that minimizes the cost function "
"starting at an initial point(s) $C(\\vec{\\theta_0})$ and move to different "
"points based on what they observe in the region they are currently "
"evaluating on successive iterations. This implies that the convergence of "
"these algorithms will usually be fast, but can be heavily dependent on the "
"initial point. Local optimizers are unable to see beyond the region where "
"they are evaluating and can be especially vulnerable to local minima, "
"reporting convergence when they find one and ignoring other states with more"
" favorable evaluations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengoptimum lokal mencari titik yang meminimumkan fungsi kos bermula dari "
"titik awal $C(\\vec{\\theta_0})$ dan bergerak ke titik lain berdasarkan apa "
"yang diperhatikan di kawasan yang sedang dinilai pada setiap lelaran. Ini "
"bermakna penumpuan algoritma ini biasanya cepat, tetapi boleh bergantung "
"sangat kepada titik awal. Pengoptimum lokal tidak dapat melihat melampaui "
"kawasan penilaian mereka dan sangat terdedah kepada minimum lokal — mereka "
"melaporkan penumpuan apabila menemuinya dan mengabaikan keadaan lain dengan "
"penilaian yang lebih baik.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Global optimizers {#global-optimizers}"
msgstr "Pengoptimum Global {#global-optimizers}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Global optimizers search for the point that minimizes the cost function over"
" several regions of its domain (that is, non-local), evaluating it "
"iteratively (that is, at iteration $i$) over a set of parameter vectors "
"$\\Theta_i := \\\\{ {\\vec\\theta_{i,j} | j \\in \\mathcal{J}_\\text{opt}^i}"
" \\\\}$ determined by the optimizer. This makes them less susceptible to "
"local minima and somewhat independent of initialization, but also "
"significantly slower to converge to a proposed solution.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengoptimum global mencari titik yang meminimumkan fungsi kos merentasi "
"beberapa kawasan domainnya (iaitu, bukan lokal), menilainya secara berulang "
"(iaitu, pada lelaran $i$) ke atas set vektor parameter $\\Theta_i := \\\\{ "
"{\\vec\\theta_{i,j} | j \\in \\mathcal{J}_\\text{opt}^i} \\\\}$ yang "
"ditentukan oleh pengoptimum. Ini menjadikannya kurang terdedah kepada "
"minimum lokal dan agak bebas daripada permulaan, tetapi juga jauh lebih "
"perlahan untuk menumpu kepada penyelesaian yang dicadangkan.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bootstrapping Optimization {#bootstrapping-optimization}"
msgstr "Pemulaan Pengoptimuman {#bootstrapping-optimization}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Bootstrapping*, or setting the initial value for parameters $\\vec\\theta$ "
"based on a prior optimization, can help our optimizer converge on a solution"
" faster. We refer to this as the initial point $\\vec\\theta_0$, and "
"$|\\psi(\\vec\\theta_0)\\rangle = U_V(\\vec\\theta_0)|\\rho\\rangle$ as the "
"initial state. This initial state differs from our reference state "
"$|\\rho\\rangle$, as the former focuses on initial parameters set during our"
" optimization loop, while the latter focuses on using known \"reference\" "
"solutions. They may coincide if $U_V(\\vec\\theta_0) \\equiv I$ (that is, "
"the identity operation).\n"
msgstr ""
"*Pemulaan*, atau menetapkan nilai awal untuk parameter $\\vec\\theta$ "
"berdasarkan pengoptimuman sebelumnya, boleh membantu pengoptimum kita "
"menumpu kepada penyelesaian dengan lebih cepat. Kita merujuknya sebagai "
"titik awal $\\vec\\theta_0$, dan $|\\psi(\\vec\\theta_0)\\rangle = "
"U_V(\\vec\\theta_0)|\\rho\\rangle$ sebagai keadaan awal. Keadaan awal ini "
"berbeza daripada keadaan rujukan kita $|\\rho\\rangle$, kerana yang pertama "
"memfokus pada parameter awal yang ditetapkan semasa gelung pengoptimuman, "
"manakala yang kedua memfokus pada penggunaan penyelesaian \"rujukan\" yang "
"diketahui. Keduanya mungkin bertepatan jika $U_V(\\vec\\theta_0) \\equiv I$ "
"(iaitu, operasi identiti).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When local optimizers converge to non-optimal local minima, we can try "
"bootstrapping the optimization globally and refine the convergence locally. "
"While this requires setting up two variational workloads, it allows the "
"optimizer to find a more optimal solution than the local optimizer alone.\n"
msgstr ""
"Apabila pengoptimum lokal menumpu kepada minimum lokal yang tidak optimum, "
"kita boleh cuba memulakan pengoptimuman secara global dan memperhalusi "
"penumpuan secara lokal. Walaupun ini memerlukan penyediaan dua beban kerja "
"variasikal, ia membolehkan pengoptimum mencari penyelesaian yang lebih "
"optimum berbanding pengoptimum lokal sahaja.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Gradient-Based and Gradient-Free Optimizers {#gradient-based-and-gradient-"
"free-optimizers}"
msgstr ""
"Pengoptimum Berasaskan Kecerunan dan Tanpa Kecerunan {#gradient-based-and-"
"gradient-free-optimizers}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Gradient-Based {#gradient-based}"
msgstr "Berasaskan Kecerunan {#gradient-based}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For our cost function $C(\\vec\\theta)$, if we have access to the gradient of the function $\\vec{\\nabla} C(\\vec\\theta)$ starting from an initial point, the simplest way to minimize the function is to update the parameters towards the direction of steepest descent of the function. That is, we update the parameters as $\\vec\\theta_{n+1} = \\vec\\theta_n - \\eta \\vec{\\nabla} C(\\vec\\theta)$, where $\\eta$ is the learning rate - a small, positive <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A hyperparameter is a parameter that we use to control our algorithm. The term hyper distinguishes it from the parameters (θ) that our algorithm is trying to find.\">hyperparameter</DefinitionTooltip> that controls the size of the update. We continue doing this until we converge to a <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A local minimum is the lowest point of the function, for a small range of values of theta. In contrast, a global minimum is the lowest point, anywhere in our function (that is, for any value of θ).\">local minimum</DefinitionTooltip> of the cost function, $C({\\vec\\theta^*})$.\n"
"We can use this cost function and an optimizer to calculate optimal parameters\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk fungsi kos $C(\\vec\\theta)$ kita, jika kita mempunyai akses kepada kecerunan fungsi $\\vec{\\nabla} C(\\vec\\theta)$ bermula dari titik awal, cara paling mudah untuk meminimumkan fungsi ialah mengemas kini parameter ke arah keturunan paling curam fungsi tersebut. Iaitu, kita mengemas kini parameter sebagai $\\vec\\theta_{n+1} = \\vec\\theta_n - \\eta \\vec{\\nabla} C(\\vec\\theta)$, di mana $\\eta$ ialah kadar pembelajaran — <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Hiperparameter ialah parameter yang kita gunakan untuk mengawal algoritma kita. Istilah 'hiper' membezakannya daripada parameter (θ) yang cuba dicari oleh algoritma kita.\">hiperparameter</DefinitionTooltip> kecil dan positif yang mengawal saiz kemas kini. Kita terus melakukan ini sehingga menumpu kepada <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Minimum lokal ialah titik terendah fungsi, untuk julat nilai theta yang kecil. Sebaliknya, minimum global ialah titik terendah di mana-mana dalam fungsi kita (iaitu, untuk sebarang nilai θ).\">minimum lokal</DefinitionTooltip> fungsi kos, $C({\\vec\\theta^*})$.\n"
"Kita boleh menggunakan fungsi kos ini dan pengoptimum untuk mengira parameter optimum\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The main disadvantages of this type of optimization are the convergence "
"speed, which can be very slow, and there is no guarantee to achieve the "
"optimal solution.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kelemahan utama jenis pengoptimuman ini ialah kelajuan penumpuan yang boleh "
"menjadi sangat perlahan, dan tiada jaminan untuk mencapai penyelesaian "
"optimum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![graph of f(theta) against theta, multiple dots show different states of a "
"gradient descent algorithm finding the minimum of a "
"curve.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/optimization-"
"loops/optimization-gradient-descent.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Graf f(theta) berbanding theta, beberapa titik menunjukkan keadaan berbeza"
" algoritma keturunan kecerunan mencari minimum "
"lengkung.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-"
"design/optimization-loops/optimization-gradient-descent.svg)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Gradient-Free {#gradient-free}"
msgstr "Tanpa Kecerunan {#gradient-free}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Gradient-free optimization algorithms do not require gradient information "
"and can be useful in situations where computing the gradient is difficult, "
"expensive, or too noisy. They also tend to be more robust in finding global "
"optima, whereas gradient-based methods tend to converge to local optima. "
"We'll explore a few instances where a gradient-free optimizer can help avoid"
" barren plateaus. However, gradient-free methods require higher "
"computational resources, especially for problems with high-dimensional "
"search spaces.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma pengoptimuman tanpa kecerunan tidak memerlukan maklumat kecerunan "
"dan berguna dalam situasi di mana mengira kecerunan adalah sukar, mahal, "
"atau terlalu bising. Ia juga cenderung lebih teguh dalam mencari optima "
"global, sedangkan kaedah berasaskan kecerunan cenderung menumpu kepada "
"optima lokal. Kita akan meneroka beberapa keadaan di mana pengoptimum tanpa "
"kecerunan boleh membantu mengelakkan dataran tandus. Namun, kaedah tanpa "
"kecerunan memerlukan sumber pengiraan yang lebih tinggi, terutamanya untuk "
"masalah dengan ruang carian berdimensi tinggi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's an example that uses the "
"[`COBYLA`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/optimize.minimize-"
"cobyla.html#optimize-minimize-cobyla) optimizer instead:\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah contoh yang menggunakan pengoptimum "
"[`COBYLA`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/optimize.minimize-"
"cobyla.html#optimize-minimize-cobyla):\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Barren Plateaus {#barren-plateaus}"
msgstr "Dataran Tandus {#barren-plateaus}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In fact, the cost landscape can be quite complicated, as shown by the hills "
"and valleys in the example below. The optimization method navigates us "
"around the cost landscape, searching for the minimum, as shown by the black "
"points and lines. We can see that two of the three searches end up in a "
"local minimum of the landscape, rather than a global one.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebenarnya, landskap kos boleh menjadi agak rumit, seperti yang ditunjukkan "
"oleh bukit-bukau dan lembah dalam contoh di bawah. Kaedah pengoptimuman "
"mengemudi kita merentasi landskap kos, mencari minimum, seperti yang "
"ditunjukkan oleh titik dan garis hitam. Kita dapat melihat bahawa dua "
"daripada tiga pencarian berakhir di minimum lokal landskap, bukan minimum "
"global.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A complicated curved manifold with many peaks and "
"troughs.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-"
"design/optimization-loops/optimization-loss-landscape.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Manifold berlengkung yang rumit dengan banyak puncak dan "
"lembah.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/optimization-"
"loops/optimization-loss-landscape.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Regardless of the type of optimization method used, if the cost landscape is"
" relatively flat, it can be challenging for the method to determine the "
"appropriate direction to search. This scenario is referred to as a "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"When gradients of parametrized quantum "
"circuits become exponentially small with respect to the number of qubits, "
"making optimization difficult and potentially impossible.\">barren "
"plateau,</DefinitionTooltip> where the cost landscape becomes progressively "
"flatter (and thus more challenging to determine the direction to the "
"minimum). For a broad range of parameterized quantum circuits, the "
"probability that the gradient along any reasonable direction is non-zero to "
"some fixed precision decreases exponentially as the number of qubits "
"increases.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tanpa mengira jenis kaedah pengoptimuman yang digunakan, jika landskap kos "
"agak rata, kaedah tersebut mungkin sukar menentukan arah carian yang sesuai."
" Senario ini dirujuk sebagai <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Apabila "
"kecerunan litar kuantum berparameter menjadi kecil secara eksponen terhadap "
"bilangan qubit, menjadikan pengoptimuman sukar dan mungkin "
"mustahil.\">dataran tandus,</DefinitionTooltip> di mana landskap kos menjadi"
" semakin rata (dan dengan itu semakin sukar untuk menentukan arah ke "
"minimum). Untuk pelbagai litar kuantum berparameter, kebarangkalian bahawa "
"kecerunan di mana-mana arah yang munasabah bukan sifar kepada ketepatan "
"tetap tertentu berkurangan secara eksponen apabila bilangan qubit "
"meningkat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A diagram of a geographic plateau compared to a slope of a mountain, to "
"explain why a gradient helps us find a minimum and a plateau hinders our "
"efforts.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-"
"design/optimization-loops/optimization-barren-plateaus.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Rajah dataran geografi berbanding cerun gunung, untuk menjelaskan mengapa "
"kecerunan membantu kita mencari minimum dan dataran menghalang usaha "
"kita.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/optimization-"
"loops/optimization-barren-plateaus.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While this area is still under active research, we have a few "
"recommendations to improve optimization performance:\n"
msgstr ""
"Walaupun kawasan ini masih dalam penyelidikan aktif, kita ada beberapa "
"cadangan untuk meningkatkan prestasi pengoptimuman:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Bootstrapping** can help the optimization loop avoid getting stuck in a "
"parameter space where the gradient is small.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pemulaan** boleh membantu gelung pengoptimuman mengelak daripada tersekat "
"dalam ruang parameter di mana kecerunan adalah kecil.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Experimenting with hardware-efficient ansatz**: Since we're using a noisy "
"quantum system as a black-box oracle, the quality of those evaluations can "
"affect the optimizer's performance. Using hardware-efficient ansatz, such as"
" "
"[`EfficientSU2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.EfficientSU2),"
" may avoid producing exponentially small gradients.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Bereksperimen dengan ansatz cekap perkakasan**: Memandangkan kita "
"menggunakan sistem kuantum berbising sebagai oracle kotak hitam, kualiti "
"penilaian tersebut boleh mempengaruhi prestasi pengoptimum. Menggunakan "
"ansatz cekap perkakasan, seperti "
"[`EfficientSU2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.EfficientSU2),"
" mungkin dapat mengelakkan penjanaan kecerunan yang kecil secara eksponen.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Experimenting with error suppression and error mitigation**:  the Qiskit "
"Runtime primitives provide a simple interface to experiment with various "
"values for `optimization_level` and `resilience_setting`, respectively. This"
" can reduce the impact of noise and make the optimization process more "
"efficient.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Bereksperimen dengan penindasan ralat dan pengurangan ralat**: primitif "
"Qiskit Runtime menyediakan antara muka mudah untuk bereksperimen dengan "
"pelbagai nilai `optimization_level` dan `resilience_setting` masing-masing. "
"Ini boleh mengurangkan kesan bunyi dan menjadikan proses pengoptimuman lebih"
" cekap.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Experimenting with gradient-free optimizers**: Unlike gradient-based "
"optimization algorithms, optimizers such as `COBYLA` do not rely on gradient"
" information to optimize the parameters and are therefore less likely to be "
"affected by the barren plateau.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Bereksperimen dengan pengoptimum tanpa kecerunan**: Tidak seperti "
"algoritma pengoptimuman berasaskan kecerunan, pengoptimum seperti `COBYLA` "
"tidak bergantung pada maklumat kecerunan untuk mengoptimumkan parameter dan "
"oleh itu kurang mungkin dipengaruhi oleh dataran tandus.\n"

